Chapter I General Provisions

Article 1 (Purpose) The purpose of this Rule is to prescribe matters delegated by the Act on Management of Disaster Management Resources and the Enforcement Decree of that Act, and matters necessary for their enforcement.

Article 2 (Management of Designated Management Institutions)
(1) Where the head of the institution operating the National Information Center for Integrated Management of Disaster Management Resources (hereinafter referred to as the "National Integrated Resource Management Information Center") designated under Article 47 (2) of the Act on Management of Disaster Management Resources (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") (hereinafter referred to as the "information center operating institution") receives, under Article 4 (3) of the Enforcement Decree of the Act on Management of Disaster Management Resources (hereinafter referred to as the "Decree"), notice of the status of management institutions designated by the heads of central administrative agencies and local governments under Article 4 (1) and (2) of the Decree (hereinafter referred to as "designated management institutions"), the head shall enter it without delay in the integrated disaster management resource management system under Article 46 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "integrated resource management system").
(2) Where data are necessary to manage information on the status of designated management institutions, the head of the information center operating institution may request the head of a designated management institution to submit such data or enter them in the integrated resource management system. In such cases, the head of the designated management institution shall comply with the request unless there is a special reason not to do so.

Chapter II Supply Chain Management Framework and Disaster Management Logistics Framework

Article 3 (Public Invitation for National Disaster Management Support Enterprises)
(1) Where the Minister of the Interior and Safety and the heads of relevant central administrative agencies determined and publicly notified by the Minister of the Interior and Safety under the main clause of Article 59 (1) of the Decree, excluding its subparagraphs (hereinafter referred to as "entrusted central administrative agencies"), intend to designate national disaster management support enterprises through a public invitation under Article 7 (2) of the Decree, they shall publish the following matters on an Internet website or by other means for at least 14 days:
1. Schedule of the public invitation;
2. Eligibility to participate in the public invitation;
3. Duties of the national disaster management support enterprise;
4. Guidelines for preparing a duty performance plan;
5. Other matters necessary for the public invitation procedure.
(2) Details concerning the public invitation procedure for national disaster management support enterprises under paragraph (1) shall be determined by the Minister of the Interior and Safety and the heads of entrusted central administrative agencies (hereinafter referred to as "national support enterprise designating authorities").

Article 4 (Issuance of Certificates of Designation of National Disaster Management Support Enterprises)
(1) Where a national support enterprise designating authority designates a national disaster management support enterprise under Article 9 (1) of the Act, it shall issue a certificate of designation of a national disaster management support enterprise in attached Form 1 (including electronic issuance through the integrated resource management system; hereinafter the same shall apply).
(2) A national support enterprise designating authority shall enter the following matters concerning a national disaster management support enterprise designated under paragraph (1) (hereinafter referred to as a "national disaster management support enterprise") in the integrated resource management system and disclose them to the public by posting them on an Internet website or by other means. In such cases, the national support enterprise designating authority shall notify the head of the information center operating institution (including the Minister of the Interior and Safety where the notifying authority is the head of an entrusted central administrative agency), in writing, of the designation of the national disaster management support enterprise, and the head of the information center operating institution shall verify the matters entered in the integrated resource management system:
1. Date and number of designation;
2. Name of the corporation and location of its principal office;
3. Name of its representative;
4. Main telephone number and Internet website address;
5. Duties arising from designation;
6. Other matters necessary for the national disaster management support enterprise to perform its duties.
(3) Where the name of the corporation or the location of its principal office changes, a national disaster management support enterprise shall submit an application for changes to the designated particulars of a national disaster management support enterprise in attached Form 2, accompanied by documents evidencing those changes, to the national support enterprise designating authority.
(4) Upon receiving an application for changes under paragraph (3), a national support enterprise designating authority shall verify its contents and reissue a certificate of designation of a national disaster management support enterprise in attached Form 1. In such cases, paragraph (2) shall apply mutatis mutandis to entry, public disclosure, notification and verification of the changes.

Article 5 (Mark for National Disaster Management Support Enterprises) The mark indicating designation as a national disaster management support enterprise under Article 9 (3) of the Act shall be as specified in attached Table 1.

Article 6 (Public Invitation for Regional Disaster Management Support Enterprises)
(1) Where a Special Metropolitan City Mayor, Metropolitan City Mayor, Special Self-Governing City Mayor, Do Governor or Special Self-Governing Province Governor (hereinafter referred to as a "Mayor/Do Governor") intends to designate regional disaster management support enterprises through a public invitation under Article 10 (2) of the Decree, the Mayor/Do Governor shall publish the following matters on an Internet website or by other means for at least 14 days:
1. Schedule of the public invitation;
2. Eligibility to participate in the public invitation;
3. Duties of the regional disaster management support enterprise;
4. Guidelines for preparing a duty performance plan;
5. Other matters necessary for the public invitation procedure.
(2) Details concerning the public invitation procedure for regional disaster management support enterprises under paragraph (1) shall be determined by the Mayor/Do Governor.

Article 7 (Issuance of Certificates of Designation of Regional Disaster Management Support Enterprises)
(1) Where a Mayor/Do Governor designates a regional disaster management support enterprise under Article 12 (1) of the Act, the Mayor/Do Governor shall issue a certificate of designation of a regional disaster management support enterprise in attached Form 3.
(2) A Mayor/Do Governor shall enter the following matters concerning a regional disaster management support enterprise designated under paragraph (1) (hereinafter referred to as a "regional disaster management support enterprise") in the integrated resource management system and disclose them to the public by posting them on an Internet website or by other means. In such cases, the Mayor/Do Governor shall notify the Minister of the Interior and Safety and the head of the information center operating institution, in writing, of the designation of the regional disaster management support enterprise, and the head of the information center operating institution shall verify the matters entered in the integrated resource management system:
1. Date and number of designation;
2. Name of the corporation and location of its principal office;
3. Name of its representative;
4. Main telephone number and Internet website address;
5. Duties arising from designation;
6. Other matters necessary for the regional disaster management support enterprise to perform its duties.
(3) Where the name of the corporation or the location of its principal office changes, a regional disaster management support enterprise shall submit an application for changes to the designated particulars of a regional disaster management support enterprise in attached Form 4, accompanied by documents evidencing those changes, to the Mayor/Do Governor.
(4) Upon receiving an application for changes under paragraph (3), a Mayor/Do Governor shall verify its contents and reissue a certificate of designation of a regional disaster management support enterprise in attached Form 3. In such cases, paragraph (2) shall apply mutatis mutandis to entry, public disclosure, notification and verification of the changes.

Article 8 (Public Invitation for National Disaster Management Logistics Enterprises)
(1) Where the Minister of the Interior and Safety intends to designate national disaster management logistics enterprises through a public invitation under Article 13 (2) of the Decree, the Minister shall publish the following matters on an Internet website or by other means for at least 14 days:
1. Schedule of the public invitation;
2. Eligibility to participate in the public invitation;
3. Duties of the national disaster management logistics enterprise;
4. Guidelines for preparing a duty performance plan;
5. Other matters necessary for the public invitation procedure.
(2) Details concerning the public invitation procedure for national disaster management logistics enterprises under paragraph (1) shall be determined by the Minister of the Interior and Safety.

Article 9 (Issuance of Certificates of Designation of National Disaster Management Logistics Enterprises)
(1) Where the Minister of the Interior and Safety designates a national disaster management logistics enterprise under Article 17 (1) of the Act, the Minister shall issue a certificate of designation of a national disaster management logistics enterprise in attached Form 5.
(2) The Minister of the Interior and Safety shall enter the following matters concerning a national disaster management logistics enterprise designated under paragraph (1) (hereinafter referred to as a "national disaster management logistics enterprise") in the integrated resource management system and disclose them to the public by posting them on an Internet website or by other means. In such cases, the Minister of the Interior and Safety shall notify the head of the information center operating institution, in writing, of the designation of the national disaster management logistics enterprise, and the head of the information center operating institution shall verify the matters entered in the integrated resource management system:
1. Date and number of designation;
2. Name of the corporation and location of its principal office;
3. Name of its representative;
4. Main telephone number and Internet website address;
5. Duties arising from designation;
6. Other matters necessary for the national disaster management logistics enterprise to perform its duties.
(3) Where the name of the corporation or the location of its principal office changes, a national disaster management logistics enterprise shall submit an application for changes to the designated particulars of a national disaster management logistics enterprise in attached Form 6, accompanied by documents evidencing those changes, to the Minister of the Interior and Safety.
(4) Upon receiving an application for changes under paragraph (3), the Minister of the Interior and Safety shall verify its contents and reissue a certificate of designation of a national disaster management logistics enterprise in attached Form 5. In such cases, paragraph (2) shall apply mutatis mutandis to entry, public disclosure, notification and verification of the changes.

Article 10 (Mark for National Disaster Management Logistics Enterprises) The mark indicating designation as a national disaster management logistics enterprise under Article 17 (3) of the Act shall be as specified in attached Table 2.

Chapter III Personnel for Management of Disaster Management Resources

Article 11 (Education of Resource Management Officers and Other Officers)
(1) Specialized education on management of disaster management resources under Article 24 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "specialized education") shall be divided into specialized education for managers and specialized education for practitioners.
(2) Persons eligible for specialized education for managers and specialized education for practitioners under paragraph (1) shall be as follows:
1. Specialized education for managers: the following persons:
(a) Resource management officers;
(b) Public officials or employees assigned part of the duties of resource management officers under Article 23 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "public officials and employees");
(c) Public officials and employees acting on behalf of resource management officers under Article 23 (2) of the Act;
2. Specialized education for practitioners: the following persons:
(a) Resource receipt and issue officers;
(b) Resource utilization officers;
(c) Public officials and employees assigned part of the duties of resource receipt and issue officers under Article 23 (1) of the Act;
(d) Public officials and employees acting on behalf of resource receipt and issue officers or resource utilization officers under Article 23 (2) of the Act.
(3) Persons eligible for specialized education under paragraph (2) shall undergo initial education within six months after assuming the relevant duties.
(4) A person who has undergone initial specialized education for managers under paragraph (2) 1 pursuant to paragraph (3) shall undergo education as needed as determined by the head of the management institution; a person who has undergone initial specialized education for practitioners under paragraph (2) 2 shall undergo regular education every two years after that initial education.
(5) The required hours of specialized education shall be as follows:
1. Specialized education for managers: at least seven hours;
2. Specialized education for practitioners: at least 14 hours.
(6) For efficient provision of specialized education, the Minister of the Interior and Safety may have the following educational institutions provide it:
1. Public official training institutions affiliated with the Ministry of the Interior and Safety, relevant central administrative agencies, or Special Metropolitan Cities, Metropolitan Cities, Special Self-Governing Cities, Dos or Special Self-Governing Provinces (hereinafter referred to as "Cities/Dos");
2. Educational institutions affiliated with disaster management responsible agencies (limited to institutions other than administrative agencies).
(7) Details concerning specialized education under paragraphs (1) through (6) shall be determined by the Minister of the Interior and Safety.

Chapter IV Management of Disaster Management Goods

Article 12 (Standards for Disaster Management Goods)
(1) When establishing institutional standards under Article 20 (1) of the Decree (hereinafter referred to as "institutional standards") and national standards under paragraph (2) of that Article (hereinafter referred to as "national standards"), or selecting or using the standards or criteria in the subparagraphs of paragraph (3) of that Article as institutional standards and national standards (hereinafter referred to as "disaster management goods standards") pursuant to that paragraph, the heads of management institutions and the Minister of the Interior and Safety shall consider the functionality, standardization, economic efficiency, up-to-dateness and other characteristics of disaster management goods.
(2) The heads of management institutions and the Minister of the Interior and Safety shall establish or amend disaster management goods standards no later than 30 days before their application, taking into account the time when disaster management goods are needed, their quality and other matters. In such cases, they shall prepare a disaster management goods standards statement in attached Form 7.
(3) Upon amending institutional standards, the head of a management institution shall submit the amended institutional standards to the Minister of the Interior and Safety without delay; upon abolishing institutional standards, the head shall notify the Minister of the Interior and Safety thereof in writing without delay.
(4) The Minister of the Interior and Safety may consult with the Administrator of the Public Procurement Service if the Minister deems it necessary for preparing a disaster management goods standards statement under the latter part of paragraph (2).

Article 13 (Analysis and Testing of Disaster Management Goods)
(1) Where the heads of management institutions and the Minister of the Interior and Safety intend to establish or amend disaster management goods standards, they may conduct the necessary analysis and testing of disaster management goods.
(2) The heads of management institutions and the Minister of the Interior and Safety may commission a reputable specialized institution or research institution to conduct all or part of the analysis and testing of disaster management goods under paragraph (1) and to prepare a disaster management goods standards statement under the latter part of Article 12 (2).
(3) Expenses incurred in the analysis and testing and preparation of disaster management goods standards statements under paragraph (2) shall be borne by the respective heads of management institutions and the Minister of the Interior and Safety.

Article 14 (Standard Forms for Stockpiling and Management of Disaster Management Goods)
(1) Standard forms under Article 28 (3) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "standard forms") shall be as follows:
1. Register of acquisition and disposal of disaster management goods in attached Form 8;
2. Disaster management goods management register in attached Form 9;
3. Disaster management goods requisition in attached Form 10;
4. Disaster management goods issue voucher in attached Form 11;
5. Disaster management goods return and receipt voucher in attached Form 12.
(2) The acquisition price shall be entered in the standard forms; where there is no acquisition price or it is unclear, the market price, appraised value under the Act on Appraisal and Certified Appraisers, or a price based on a quotation shall be entered. Provided, That in the disaster management goods management register among the standard forms, where goods have been valued according to any of the following standards, that value shall be entered:
1. National accounting standards under Article 11 of the National Accounting Act;
2. Local accounting standards under Article 12 of the Local Accounting Act;
3. Institutional accounting standards equivalent to those in subparagraphs 1 and 2 (limited to management institutions other than administrative agencies under Article 2, subparagraph 1 of the Decree).
(3) The acquisition price under the main clause of paragraph (2), excluding its subparagraphs, shall include the price of the disaster management goods and fees, installation expenses, transportation expenses and incidental expenses otherwise incurred in connection with their purchase.
(4) When entering the status of disaster management goods in the standard forms, the rules for recording disaster management goods in attached Table 3 shall apply.
(5) Where a resource management officer, resource receipt and issue officer or resource utilization officer is replaced, the predecessor shall prepare the standard forms to be handed over and a handover statement as of the day preceding the date of replacement, and hand them over to the successor. Provided, That where there is an unavoidable reason why the predecessor cannot carry out the handover procedure, the successor shall prepare the standard forms and a statement of reasons and affix the successor's name and seal to the statement of reasons.

Article 15 (Stockpile Management Standards for Disaster Management Goods) When establishing stockpile management standards under Article 23 of the Decree, the Minister of the Interior and Safety and the heads of management institutions shall use information on demand forecasts and other matters provided by the integrated resource management system and shall clearly specify the catalog number, name, item, quantity and other necessary particulars of disaster management goods.

Article 16 (Inventory Surveys of Disaster Management Goods)
(1) When conducting a regular inventory survey under Article 30 (1) of the Act and Article 26 (2) of the Decree, the head of a management institution shall appoint as inventory survey officers public officials and employees not directly involved in duties concerning management of the relevant disaster management goods.
(2) Where the head of a management institution intends to conduct an ad hoc inventory survey under Article 30 (1) of the Act and Article 26 (4) of the Decree, the head shall have resource management officers or resource receipt and issue officers conduct an inventory survey of the disaster management goods under their jurisdiction.
(3) When conducting an inventory survey under paragraphs (1) and (2), the head of a management institution shall have the inventory survey officers under paragraph (1) and the resource management officers and resource receipt and issue officers under paragraph (2) classify the condition of the disaster management goods according to attached Table 4.

Article 17 (Special Inventory Surveys)
(1) Where the Minister of the Interior and Safety and a Mayor/Do Governor intend to conduct a special inventory survey under Article 30 (2) of the Act and Article 26 (5) of the Decree, they shall establish guidelines for the special inventory survey containing the following matters and notify the head of the relevant management institution no later than one month before the survey reference date:
1. Basic direction of the special inventory survey;
2. Organization of special inventory survey teams;
3. Period of the special inventory survey;
4. Other matters necessary for the special inventory survey.
(2) Article 16 (3) shall apply mutatis mutandis to classification of the condition of disaster management goods when conducting a special inventory survey under paragraph (1).

Article 18 (Inventory Adjustments for Disaster Management Goods)
(1) Where a resource management officer discovers an increase or decrease in disaster management goods as a result of an inventory survey or special inventory survey under Article 30 (1) and (2) of the Act, the officer shall ascertain the cause of the increase or decrease without delay and apply to the head of the management institution to which the officer belongs for approval of an inventory adjustment under Article 30 (4) of the Act by submitting an application for approval of an inventory adjustment for disaster management goods in attached Form 13 accompanied by the following documents:
1. Two copies of the management register for the disaster management goods subject to the inventory adjustment;
2. Two copies of the inventory survey statement of increases and decreases for the disaster management goods subject to the inventory adjustment;
3. Two copies of other relevant evidentiary documents (documents proving that the discrepancy arose from an administrative error).
(2) Upon obtaining approval under paragraph (1), a resource management officer shall have the resource receipt and issue officer enter the approval date, grounds for approval and document number in the remarks column of the standard forms and other records for the relevant disaster management goods and update those forms and records.
(3) Disaster management goods for which approval under paragraph (1) has not been obtained shall be treated as damaged or lost in accordance with Article 47 of the Enforcement Decree of the Goods Management Act or as determined by the head of the management institution.

Article 19 (Transfer of Management of Disaster Management Goods)
(1) Where a resource management officer transfers management of disaster management goods under the officer's jurisdiction pursuant to Article 30 (5) of the Act and Article 28 of the Decree, the officer shall order the resource receipt and issue officer holding the goods to issue them and shall order the resource utilization officer using the goods to return them.
(2) When ordering return under paragraph (1), a resource management officer shall clearly identify to the resource utilization officer the person who is to receive the disaster management goods and order their delivery.
(3) Where a resource management officer transfers management of disaster management goods under the officer's jurisdiction, the officer shall notify the other resource management officer receiving the transfer of management of the person delivering the goods, the time and place of delivery, the names of the goods and other necessary particulars.
(4) A resource management officer notified under paragraph (3) shall order the resource receipt and issue officer to receive the disaster management goods into stock.
(5) Where an institution or department intending to receive a transfer of management wishes to inspect the relevant disaster management goods, the resource management officer shall cooperate.
(6) Where a resource utilization officer returns disaster management goods pursuant to an order to return them under paragraph (1), the resource management officer may reclassify their condition according to attached Table 4.

Article 20 (Matters Concerning Maintenance of Disaster Management Goods) "Matters prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety" in Article 29 (4) of the Decree means the following:
1. Types and names of disaster management goods;
2. Catalog numbers of disaster management goods;
3. Maintenance period;
4. Maintenance location;
5. Names, addresses and emergency contact networks of suppliers or specialized maintenance firms (limited to cases where maintenance has been commissioned to a supplier, specialized maintenance firm or other entity under Article 29 (3) of the Decree).

Article 21 (Criteria for Decisions to Declare Goods Unserviceable)
(1) Disaster management goods for which a decision to declare goods unserviceable under Article 36 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a "decision of unserviceability") may be made shall be as follows:
1. Disaster management goods that no longer need to be used and are not expected to be used in the future;
2. Disaster management goods that have exceeded their useful life and disaster management goods held in stock in excess of demand for a foreseeable period;
3. Disaster management goods for which the original equipment can no longer be used or no longer exists, where there is neither a need nor a possibility to acquire such equipment anew;
4. Disaster management goods that are difficult to repair because their specifications or models have changed, or cannot be used for their original purpose even if repaired;
5. Disaster management goods removed from facilities that cannot be utilized;
6. Disaster management goods that have been damaged or worn out and cannot be used for their original purpose even if repaired;
7. Disaster management goods requiring repair where repair would be uneconomical;
8. Disaster management goods mobilized under Articles 49 through 52 of the Act for which a decision of unserviceability is necessary for gratuitous transfer under Article 39 (1) of the Act;
9. Disaster management goods provided as assistance under Articles 44 and 46 of the Framework Act on the Management of Disasters and Safety and Article 8 of the Administrative Procedures Act for which a decision of unserviceability is necessary for gratuitous transfer under Article 39 (1) of the Act;
10. Other disaster management goods that the head of a management institution deems to be subject to reasons equivalent to those in subparagraphs 1 through 9.
(2) When making a decision of unserviceability, a resource management officer shall prepare a decision of unserviceability (request for approval) in attached Form 14 and, for disaster management goods subject to approval under Article 37 (1) of the Decree (hereinafter referred to as "goods subject to approval"), shall request approval of the decision of unserviceability from the head of the management institution. Provided, That for goods subject to approval among disaster management goods falling under paragraph (1) 8 and 9, approval of a decision of unserviceability may be requested after mobilization or provision of assistance using those goods has ended.

Article 22 (Eligible Purchasers of Disaster Management Goods)
(1) "Persons prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety" in Article 38 (2) 3 of the Decree means enterprises or institutions falling under any of the following:
1. National disaster management support enterprises;
2. Regional disaster management support enterprises;
3. National disaster management logistics enterprises;
4. Management institutions.
(2) "Management institutions prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety" in Article 38 (2) 4 of the Decree means management institutions required to bear mobilization expenses under Article 53 (1) of the Act.

Chapter V Management of Disaster Management Property and Disaster Management Personnel

Article 23 (Matters to Be Recorded and Maintained for Disaster Management Property) "Matters prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety" in Article 44 (1) 6 of the Decree means the following:
1. Status of formulation and submission of disaster management property management plans under Article 41 of the Act and Article 42 of the Decree;
2. Records of settlement of mobilization expenses under Article 53 of the Act and Article 54 of the Decree;
3. Other matters determined by the Minister of the Interior and Safety as necessary for management of disaster management property.

Article 24 (Matters to Be Recorded and Maintained for Disaster Management Personnel) "Matters prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety" in Article 47 (1) 7 of the Decree means the following:
1. Status of formulation and submission of disaster management personnel management plans under Article 43 of the Act and Article 45 of the Decree;
2. Records of settlement of mobilization expenses under Article 53 of the Act and Article 54 of the Decree;
3. Other matters determined by the Minister of the Interior and Safety as necessary for management of disaster management personnel.

Chapter VI Integrated Management of Disaster Management Resources

Article 25 (Establishment and Operation of the Integrated Resource Management System) "Information prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety" in Article 46 (1) 11 of the Act means the following:
1. Information on maintenance records of disaster management goods under Article 31 of the Act;
2. Information on stockpiling facilities under Article 33 (1) of the Act;
3. Information on establishment and operation of regional integrated disaster management resource management centers under Article 45 of the Act;
4. Information on expenses for mobilizing disaster management resources under Article 53 of the Act;
5. Other information concerning disaster management resources that the Minister of the Interior and Safety deems necessary to manage.

Article 26 (Application for Designation as an Information Center Operating Institution)
(1) An application for designation as an information center operating institution under Article 51 (2) of the Decree shall be in attached Form 15.
(2) The following documents shall accompany an application for designation under paragraph (1):
1. Documents proving eligibility under Article 47 (2) 2 or 3 of the Act;
2. An operating plan concerning the standards and qualifications necessary to perform the duties;
3. A business plan and summary concerning establishment of the integrated resource management system and operation of the National Integrated Resource Management Information Center.

Article 27 (Examination for Designation as an Information Center Operating Institution)
(1) Where two or more institutions or organizations submit applications for designation under Article 26, the Minister of the Interior and Safety shall establish an examination committee and designate the most suitable institution or organization as the information center operating institution following a fair examination.
(2) The examination committee under paragraph (1) shall consist of at least eight members, including one chairperson. Members shall be designated or commissioned by the Minister of the Interior and Safety from among public officials of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety and persons with expertise in information technology, logistics and distribution, disaster management or other relevant fields. Commissioned members shall constitute a majority of all members.
(3) Details concerning the composition and operation of the examination committee under paragraph (2) shall be determined by the Minister of the Interior and Safety.

Article 28 (Certificate of Designation as an Information Center Operating Institution) A certificate of designation as an information center operating institution under Article 52 of the Decree shall be in attached Form 16.

Chapter VII Mobilization of Disaster Management Resources

Article 29 (Mobilization Orders) An order for mobilization of disaster management resources under Article 53 of the Decree shall be issued using a disaster management resource mobilization order in attached Form 17.

Chapter VIII Supplementary Provisions

Article 30 (Management Inspections) When conducting a management inspection under Article 57 of the Decree, the head of a management institution shall designate inspecting public officials and employees from among those who are not in charge of management duties for the disaster management resources subject to inspection.

