| 2. Unusable disaster management goods | (a) Scrap goods | Disaster management goods for which repair and use would not be economical (goods for which repair expenses exceed the economic limit); disaster management goods that cannot be repaired; disaster management goods left over after use that cannot be utilized again |

Note
The condition of disaster management goods shall be classified by sensory inspection [meaning an inspection using the five human senses; hereinafter the same shall apply]. Provided, That where it is difficult to classify their condition by sensory inspection, methods such as performance testing or physical and chemical testing may be used.

